      "side": 1,
      "message": "The ec-mkbp-host-event-wakeup-mask node is used to set the CONFIG_MKBP_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK macro, so it doesn\u0027t use host_event_set_bit().\n\ntrogdor/baseboard.h has this define, which uses the EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK transformation:\n#define CONFIG_MKBP_HOST_EVENT_WAKEUP_MASK \\\n\t\t(EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_LID_OPEN) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_POWER_BUTTON) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_AC_CONNECTED) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_AC_DISCONNECTED) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_HANG_DETECT) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_RTC) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE) | \\\n\t\t EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK(EC_HOST_EVENT_DEVICE))\n\nSo the ec-mkbp-host-event-wakeup-mask needs a similar transformation.\n\nI do suggest moving this macro to be adjacent to the HOST_EVENT_ defines below.  I also suggest renaming to HOST_EVENT_MASK to match the existing naming convention and prevent from overloading EC_HOST_EVENT_MASK.",
